//? Title: Partial inpainting:mask propagation and visible full-objective optimization
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Generate source-identical irregular CIFAR masks with tensor geometry,then explain partial-convolution renormalization,mask propagation and dilated-hole L1 TV. Run full/compact U-Nets,genuine frozen VGG16 feature losses and every one of48 Adam updates. Restore an image+mask-only predictor with immutable learned/BN values and compare all16 held-out reconstructions against the observed-only mean reference.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/partial_inpainting.cpp`.

> The method

Original observed RGB and validity are the only forward inputs. Every partial convolution masks,renormalizes and propagates support;both features and masks travel through U-Net skips. The report explicitly owns the complete pixel/perceptual/style/TV objective,optimizer and paired validation checkpoint. Tensor mask geometry,independent native/Keras derivatives and actual image/error previews make the short experiment reproducible.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/partial_inpainting_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/partial_inpainting_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/partial_inpainting_concept.tikz > build/partial_inpainting_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/partial_inpainting_concept.svg build/partial_inpainting_concept.dvi > build/partial_inpainting_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
