> Propagating masks makes new computational support explicit

Each supported output becomes mask1 for the next layer,so support can
expand into a hole. It does not turn those locations into measured pixels:
the propagated features remain model computations. A U-Net nearest-upsamples
and concatenates both feature and mask skips. The final skip includes the
original observed RGB and mask. This fixture follows a25-pixel hole through
three genuine partial convolutions with fixed weights.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/partial_inpainting_support.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto axis = n::arange(0, 9), yy = axis.reshape({1, 9, 1, 1}),
             xx = axis.reshape({1, 1, 9, 1}),
             hole = n::logical_and(n::logical_and(n::greater_equal(yy, 2.), n::less(yy, 7.)),
                                   n::logical_and(n::greater_equal(xx, 2.), n::less(xx, 7.)));
  const auto original = n::logical_not(hole).to(n::DType::Float32);
  auto mask = original, image = n::ones({1, 9, 9, 1});
  std::print("Unsupported pixels:{}",
             n::count_nonzero(n::equal(mask, 0.)).item<std::int64_t>());
  for (int stage = 1; stage <= 3; ++stage) {
    const auto out =
        m::PartialConv(image, mask, n::ones({3, 3, 1, 1}), n::zeros({1}), 1, 1, 3);
    image = out.value;
    mask = out.mask;
    std::print(" ->{}", n::count_nonzero(n::equal(mask, 0.)).item<std::int64_t>());
  }
  std::print(". New support is computed,not new sensor truth.\n");
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(original.reshape({9, 9}), {0}), 0, 1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(mask.reshape({9, 9}), {0}), 0, 1);
  a.title("Original observed support").x_label("source column").y_label("row0 at bottom");
  b.title("After three masked convolutions")
      .x_label("source column")
      .y_label("row0 at bottom");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/partial_inpainting_support.svg");
}
```
