> Full-image pixel losses and dilated-hole total variation

The complete objective is valid+6*hole+.05*perceptual+
120*(style_raw+style_composite)+.1*TV. Valid/hole pixel L1 losses divide
by the full RGB image size,not their own support counts. Perceptual L1
compares raw and observed-preserving composites with truth at VGG16
pool1/2/3. Style uses channel/spatial-normalized Grams and L1 distances.

Genuine Keras VGG uses centered BGR255;this source then divides pooled
activations by255. These feature units are explicit and are not a claim
of pretrained Torch parity. TV is L1 over neighbors whose both endpoints
lie in a one-pixel-dilated hole,divided by full image size. The fixture shows
original versus dilated hole support and the actual raw-image adjoints.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/partial_inpainting_tv.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto yy = n::arange(0, 6).reshape({1, 6, 1, 1}),
             xx = n::arange(0, 8).reshape({1, 1, 8, 1}),
             hole = n::logical_and(n::logical_and(n::greater_equal(yy, 2.), n::less(yy, 4.)),
                                   n::logical_and(n::greater_equal(xx, 3.), n::less(xx, 6.)));
  const auto mask = n::ones({1, 6, 8, 3}) * n::logical_not(hole).to(n::DType::Float32),
             truth = n::full({1, 6, 8, 3}, .4),
             raw = n::full({1, 6, 8, 3}, .8).requires_grad_(),
             comp = m::PartialComposite(truth, raw, mask),
             region = n::max_pool2d(1. - mask, 3, 1, n::Padding::Same),
             tv = m::PartialTV(comp, mask), g = n::grad(tv, {raw})[0];
  std::print("Full-image valid/hole L1 {:.6f}/{:.6f};hole-region TV {:.6f};known raw adjoints "
             "max {:.3g}.\n",
             n::mean(mask * n::abs(raw - truth)).item(),
             n::mean((1. - mask) * n::abs(raw - truth)).item(), tv.item(),
             n::max(n::abs(g) * mask).item());
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(hole.to(n::DType::Float32).reshape({6, 8}), {0}), 0,
                              1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(n::select(n::select(region, 0, 0), 2, 0), {0}), 0, 1);
  a.title("True original hole pixels").x_label("original column").y_label("row0 at bottom");
  b.title("One-pixel dilated TV region").x_label("original column").y_label("row0 at bottom");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/partial_inpainting_tv.svg");
}
```
