// result_end
\caption(All48 visible Adam updates use the complete seven-component source objective. Right-panel weighted components sum to fitting total;validation uses inference BN state.)
\alttext(All48 visible Adam updates use the complete seven-component source objective. Right-panel weighted components sum to fitting total;validation uses inference BN state.)


\image(figures/partial_inpainting_metrics.svg)
\caption(All16 test images compare raw composite,metric-only clipped composite,and observed-only mean fill. Both mean per-image PSNR and pooled-MSE PSNR use true original holes;negative pooled values remain visible.)
\alttext(Raw,clipped and visible-mean hole quality on identical actual test masks,with distinct PSNR aggregation policies.)

\image(figures/partial_inpainting_predictions.png)
\caption(All16 actual held-out images,two tiles per row. Each tile is observed RGB,visible-mean reference,raw composite display-clipped to unit RGB,original truth,and4x RGB-mean error in red. Numeric raw scores retain original unconstrained predictions.)
\alttext(Original held-out CIFAR contents with fixed irregular holes,observed-only means,actual image+mask-only predictions,truth and measured errors.)

The selected epoch3 lowers validation loss to357.556 and the fixed fitting
probe from544.770 to176.898. Yet raw mean hole PSNR is only.880180dB;
metric-only clipping reaches7.461787dB,still well below the observed-mean
reference14.555607dB. The raw pooled-MSE PSNR is negative. The visible
bright hole artifacts agree with this failure to improve reconstruction.

A falling full perceptual objective does not establish better reconstruction.
Compare raw and clipped scores with the observed-only reference and inspect
every held-out tile. Projection is not part of this model’s training or
prediction;clipping is explicit metric/display policy. This short compact
fit is not paper-quality or a pretrained inpainting benchmark.

> Conclusion

Independent geometry/full-objective Jacobians and genuine Keras every-pixel gradients establish the mechanisms. Forty-eight visible tensor Adam updates connect them to original images and reproducible irregular holes. Input-only restored prediction,finite hidden-fill independence and honest raw/clipped/reference scores keep the short reconstruction claim concrete.

> References

- [Liu et al.,Image Inpainting for Irregular Holes Using Partial Convolutions](https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.07723).
- [Official NVIDIA partial-convolution reference](https://github.com/NVIDIA/partialconv).
- [Official Keras VGG16 pretrained implementation](https://github.com/keras-team/keras/blob/master/keras/src/applications/vgg16.py).
